        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Job\nRole: Junior Software Engineer\nRole Type: Full-time\nExperience: 1–2 years\nCompensation: $500 USD base salary per month, plus up to $200 USD in performance-based bonuses per month.\nAbout the Role\nSmartPropFirm is looking for a Junior Software Engineer to join our Product & Engineering team.\nYou’ll help build and improve software for the prop trading industry, including trading tools, dashboards, rewards systems, marketplaces, and platform features.\nWe’re looking for someone with strong programming fundamentals who learns quickly, solves problems effectively, and is comfortable using modern development and AI tools.\nResponsibilities\nBuild and improve features across our web platform.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and reliable code.\nWork across frontend and backend based on project needs.\nIntegrate APIs, databases, and third-party services.\nFix bugs, improve performance, and test your work.\nUse AI tools effectively for development, research, and debugging.\nCollaborate with the team and take ownership of assigned tasks.\nRequirements\n1–2 years of software development experience.\nStrong programming fundamentals.\nGood knowledge of JavaScript/TypeScript, React, and Next.js.\nBasic understanding of APIs, databases, and authentication.\nComfortable with Git, code reviews, and existing codebases.\nStrong problem-solving and communication skills.\nExperience with AI development tools such as ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude, or GitHub Copilot.\nNice to Have\nExperience with Next.js, Node.js, WordPress, REST APIs, or SaaS platforms.\nFamiliarity with responsive UI/UX and production debugging.\nExperience or interest in fintech, trading, dashboards, marketplaces, or rewards systems.\nWhy Join SmartPropFirm?\nBuild real products used by traders.\nGain hands-on full-stack development experience.\nLearn from an experienced product and engineering team.\nWork with modern technologies and AI-assisted development.\nGrow quickly in a fast-moving environment where your work has direct impact.\nAdditional Requirements\n1+ years of work experience with software engineering practices.\n1+ years of work experience with Next.js.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488838083": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description\nYuzee connects people with education, careers and employment opportunities. Our platform brings together course discovery, job search, institutions, employers and AI-assisted guidance across web and mobile.\nWe’re looking for a senior, hands-on Angular developer who can take ownership of frontend delivery and help guide our technical direction. You should be comfortable understanding an existing product, identifying what needs improvement and delivering practical, reliable solutions.\nAre you a talented and experienced Angular Developer looking to be part of a dynamic and innovative team? Join us at Yuzee and contribute to the creation of cutting-edge web application that redefine user experiences.\nJob Description\nWhat you’ll do\nDevelop and improve our Angular web applications and contribute to our Ionic/Capacitor mobile app.\nOwn features from understanding requirements through implementation, testing and release verification.\nImprove important user journeys, including search, navigation, conversations, forms and account management.\nDiagnose problems across the interface, application state, APIs and data, and resolve their underlying causes.\nWork closely with backend developers to build clear API contracts, dependable integrations and useful error handling.\nHelp establish consistent architecture, reusable components, coding standards and appropriate automated tests.\nReview code, document important decisions and support other developers.\nRecommend improvements that balance product needs, maintainability, performance and delivery time.\nWhat We’re Looking For\nStrong experience delivering production applications with Angular, TypeScript, RxJS, HTML and CSS.\nA sound understanding of component design, routing, forms, state management and asynchronous behaviour.\nExperience maintaining and improving an established codebase.\nStrong skills in REST API integration, authentication, session handling and debugging.\nExperience with Git, pull requests, code reviews and automated testing.\nAttention to responsive design, accessibility and consistent behaviour across browsers and devices.\nClear communication and the ability to explain technical decisions and trade-offs.\nEvidence of taking responsibility for working software, including investigating issues after release.\nWhat Success Looks Like\nYou understand how the existing platform fits together, help the team agree on sensible priorities and deliver improvements users can depend on. Your changes preserve working journeys, reduce recurring problems and make future development easier.\nQualifications\nGood spoken and written English proficiency\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or Computer Engineering\n4 years experience with front-end development\nAt least 4 years of proven experience with Angular 7 or 8\nProven work experience investigating issues faced by users, identify the root causes and fixing them\n4 years of experience in using Agile work methodologies\nProficient in CSS, HTML, and writing cross-browser compatible codes\n4 years of extensive programming experience in HTML5, CSS3, SASS and Bootstrap\n4 years of experience with REST APIs\nKnowledge of JavaScript MV-VM/MVC frameworks including Angluar JS\nExtensive experience with Node JS and Express JS is a bonus\nGreat project management skills is a bonus\nAbility to work with a multicultural team\nExcellent communication skills\nCritical thinker and good problem-solver\nAdditional Information\nThis is a full-time remote job (You will work from home)\nChallenging work environment and complex project where you can really grow as a professional\nCompany shares can be offered based on how successful with our products' launch\nPromotions towards better job roles possible after a certain period of time",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489496365": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nRevive Business Solutions works with organizations to support business technology and software solutions. The Dealer Management Systems Integration team helps connect applications and services so that information can move reliably between systems. The team contributes to ongoing application development, maintenance, integration, and modernization, with a focus on dependable and maintainable solutions. Team members collaborate across technical and business functions to understand needs, address issues, and deliver improvements.\nAbout The Role\nRevive Business Solutions is seeking an early-career .NET Developer to support its Dealer Management Systems Integration team. This opportunity is suitable for a candidate with approximately one to three years of experience gained through professional employment, an internship, a co-op, academic work, or personal projects. You will contribute to application enhancements, maintenance, testing, API development, and integration support while learning from senior developers, product owners, and team leads.\nThe successful candidate will work through the software development lifecycle in a collaborative Agile environment. You will take on assigned development and troubleshooting tasks, participate in team practices, and build your experience with modern application development and integration. This role calls for curiosity, clear communication, accountability, and a willingness to strengthen technical skills over time.\nQualifications\nA bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Systems, or a related technical field is required. Candidates should have approximately one year or more of exposure to C#, ASP.NET, .NET Core, or object-oriented programming through work, internships, co-op placements, coursework, or projects.\nExperience or familiarity with front-end technologies such as ReactJS, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, or jQuery is valuable. Candidates should understand basic SQL queries and relational database concepts, and have exposure to creating, consuming, testing, or supporting web APIs. Familiarity with REST, JSON payloads, request and response handling, authentication concepts, and API connectivity troubleshooting is desirable; exposure to SOAP services is an asset.\nAdditional useful knowledge includes unit or API testing, debugging, Git, branching, pull requests, and code reviews. Awareness of SOLID principles, clean code, reusable components, application security, performance, scalability, and maintainability is an advantage. Familiarity with Azure DevOps, Azure DevOps Services, Jira, Azure, Kubernetes, or CI/CD concepts is welcome. Academic, open-source, internship, or personal software projects are also relevant.\nResponsibilities\nContribute to enhancements, maintenance, defect resolution, refactoring, and small feature development for existing web applications, following team standards and receiving guidance where appropriate. Assist with building and supporting APIs and integrations between internal and external systems, including data mapping, error handling, logging, and coordination with consuming applications.\nHelp test and validate code, investigate application or connectivity issues, and support data-related troubleshooting. Participate in Agile ceremonies, including sprint planning, daily stand-ups, backlog refinement, and retrospectives. Collaborate with developers, product owners, business partners, and quality assurance colleagues to clarify requirements and share progress. Follow development, deployment, and documentation practices, and contribute to continuous improvement across the software development lifecycle.\nBenefits\nThis role offers the opportunity to develop practical software engineering skills while contributing to real application and systems integration work. You will collaborate with experienced technical and business colleagues, gain exposure to APIs and the .NET ecosystem, and build familiarity with Agile delivery and modernization efforts. The team environment supports continued learning and the gradual development of technical ownership.\nEqual Opportunity\nRevive Business Solutions is committed to providing a respectful and inclusive workplace. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, skills, and business needs. We welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds and encourage candidates who meet the role requirements to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489633576": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the job\nMeeBoss is sharing this role on behalf of Prime Techwings.\nMeeBoss is sharing this active opportunity on behalf of Voltus, a leading company for Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) that aims to be the platform fulfilling the promise of the energy transition.\nThis role is appropriate for entry-level to early-career engineering candidates eager to build scalable software for Voltus.\nYou will join a fully remote team tackling complex energy industry challenges, collaborating with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack, and contributing to core systems that decarbonize the grid.\nJob title\nSoftware Engineer\nLocation\nRemote\nCompensation\nBase pay is $110,000-$140,000 USD annually, commensurate with experience, with a 10% annual bonus and equity.\nWhy this role\nJoin a fully remote team distributed across the US, Canada, and abroad.\nContribute to core systems that decarbonize the grid and provide flexibility, reliability, and resilience to the energy market.\nCollaborate with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack including Python, Postgres, Go, FastAPI, and React.\nWhat you will do\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code to support the team’s projects.\nContribute to the design and implementation of new features and services.\nCollaborate with your team to troubleshoot and resolve issues in the production environment.\nParticipate in code reviews to learn from and contribute to the team’s shared knowledge.\nWork with stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nWhat we are looking for\nA Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent combination of education and experience, in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\nFoundational programming skills in a backend language like Python.\nA strong desire to learn and grow as a software engineer.\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\nA genuine passion for creating a cleaner, more resilient energy future.\nAuthorization to work in the US or Canada without sponsorship.\nA link to your GitHub account in the application (applications without a GitHub account will not be considered).\nBenefits\nUnlimited PTO for full-time employees.\nParental leave.\nComprehensive benefits package to promote health, wellness, and financial security.\nAbout MeeBoss\nMeeBoss helps job seekers and hiring teams make direct, relevant career connections.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490035427": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nACE Money Transfer is looking for a skilled Laravel Developer to develop, maintain and optimise our web applications using PHP and the Laravel framework .\nYou will build and improve the backend services, RESTful APIs and database layers behind our digital platforms. You will also integrate third-party services and keep our applications secure, scalable and high-performing .\nYou will work closely with frontend developers, QA engineers and the wider technology team, from writing clean code and reviewing pull requests through to deployment and production support.\nThe role reports to [Insert, e.g., Engineering Manager / Tech Lead] . It suits a developer with strong backend skills who takes ownership of their work and wants to grow in a fast-moving fintech environment.\nResponsibilities\nApplication Development\nDevelop, maintain, and improve web applications using PHP and Laravel\nWrite clean, reusable, efficient, and well-structured code\nDesign, build and maintain RESTful APIs and backend services.1\nIntegrate third-party APIs and external services\nDatabase Management\nWork with MySQL databases, including database design and query optimisation\nQuality, Performance & Security\nIdentify, troubleshoot and fix application bugs and performance issues\nKeep applications secure, scalable and performing well\nTake part in code reviews and follow established coding standards\nDeployment & Production Support\nManage application deployments and support production environments\nCollaboration & Documentation\nWork with frontend developers, QA engineers, and other team members\nKeep technical documentation up to date and follow development SOPs\nRequirements\nQualifications & Experience\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field (preferred)\n2–4 years of experience in PHP and Laravel development\nStrong knowledge of PHP and Laravel\nGood understanding of MVC architecture and OOP concepts\nExperience with MySQL and database optimisation\nKnowledge of developing and integrating RESTful APIs\nProficiency in HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Bootstrap\nFamiliarity with Git and version control workflows\nUnderstanding of authentication, authorisation and application security\nExperience with debugging and performance optimisation\nPreferred:\nExperience with Laravel queues, jobs, events and scheduling\nFamiliarity with Redis and caching\nKnowledge of Linux environments and deployment processes\nExperience with third-party integrations and payment gateways\nFamiliarity with Agile/Scrum methods\nSoft Skills & Leadership\nProblem-solving: strong analytical and problem-solving skills\nCommunication and teamwork: works well with developers, QA and stakeholders\nTime management: handles several tasks at once and meets deadlines\nContinuous learning: keen to learn new technologies and build technical skills\nOwnership: works independently and takes responsibility for assigned tasks\nJob Details\nLocation: Lahore/Kharian, Pakistan\nJob Type: Onsite\nWorking Hours / Shift: 01:00 PKT to 10:00 PKT\nDepartment: Technology / Software Development\nAbout ACE Money Transfer\nACE Money Transfer is a UK-based multinational fintech headquartered in Manchester, United Kingdom. We provide fast, secure and affordable online remittance services to customers in 29 countries across the UK, Europe, Canada and Australia, and we enable cross-border money transfers to 100+ countries worldwide.\nEvery day, our platform helps people support their families, pay for education and build better futures across borders. As part of the wider ACE Group, we combine a fast-paced growth culture with strong regulatory standards and a commitment to innovation in digital payments.\nAt ACE you will work with talented, diverse teams across multiple regions and take real ownership of work that matters. You will also help shape the future of global money movement.\nLearn more: ACE Money Transfer Company Profile\nPowered by JazzHR\nQJ9QVNkoph",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00"
  },
  "cache:posts": {
    "entries": {
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/anne-ong-lightwayhrconsultancy_lightwayhr-share-7525761806112477184-W01D": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:52:19.965819+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "𝐅𝐨𝐫𝐦𝐞𝐫 𝐜𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐚𝐠𝐮𝐞𝐬 𝐜𝐚𝐧 𝐛𝐞 𝐬𝐨𝐦𝐞 𝐨𝐟 𝐨𝐮𝐫 𝐬𝐭𝐫𝐨𝐧𝐠𝐞𝐬𝐭 𝐩𝐫𝐨𝐟𝐞𝐬𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐜𝐨𝐧𝐧𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬.\n\nThey have worked with us before. They know \nhow we communicate, \nhow we work with others, \nhow we handle challenges, \nand what we bring to the table.\n\nOver the years, I have also had former colleagues connect me with opportunities in their current organisations — sometimes by making an introduction, sometimes by pointing me towards a need they felt I could help with.\n\nTo me, these introductions are meaningful because they come from people who already know how we work. There is already a level of familiarity and trust behind the connection.\n\nThis kind of referral is different from a cold introduction.\n\nAnd today, LinkedIn makes it much easier to stay connected even after people move on to different companies, industries or countries.\n\nA strong network is not built only by meeting new people. It is also built by maintaining the relationships we have already formed.\n\nSometimes opportunities do not come from the people we have just met. They come from people who already know how we work.\n\nDo you find that some of your strongest professional opportunities come from people who have worked with you before?\n\n#LightwayHR\n\n10 Nov 2026",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-10T03:30:37.116Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/haluk-sayar-34635811_cop31-zeroemissionmobility-cop31-share-7524444889644871680-0YvB": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:52:19.965819+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "At COP31, our panel From Climate Targets to Market Deployment: Scaling Zero-Emission Mobility Across Markets will explore how different markets can accelerate the rollout of zero-emission mobility.\n📅 10 November 2026, 13:30–14:15\n📍 Türkiye Pavilion, Room 3, Blue Zone\nAttendance requires COP31 Blue Zone accreditation.\n#COP31 #ZeroEmissionMobility \n \nChris Heron, Ioana Petcu, Feng An, Ph.D., Michiel Langezaal, Kristian Ruby, E-Mobility Europe, Avrasya E-Mobilite Derneği (Eski isim AVERE), Turkish Association for Energy Economics / Enerji Ekonomisi Derneği, International Association for Energy Economics",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-06T12:17:39.424Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/josephcass_breaking-brookfield-announces-huge-27-billion-share-7523323322541969408-zmpB": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:52:19.965819+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "BREAKING: Brookfield announces HUGE $27 BILLION AI data centre project in the UK! \n\nBrookfield has partnered with British energy company Drax Group and AI business Radiant to develop one of the UK’s largest AI data centres at Drax Power Station in the north of England. \n\nBloomberg reports that the project could attract more than $27 Billion billion in investment, with an initial $3.3 Billion planned for the first phase, backed by Brookfield’s partnership with the Qatar Investment Authority.\n\nThe idea is to build the data centre alongside an existing power station, giving it access to the enormous amounts of electricity needed to run AI technology. Drax CEO Will Gardiner said: “If constructed in full, this project could become one of the largest data centres in the UK.” Brookfield's Connor Teskey recently said of AI infrastructure: \"there is no shortage of capital - and there is no shortage of demand.\"\n\nBig news for European AI infrastructure!\n\nFollow Joseph Cass for finance news and insights.",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-03T10:00:57.048Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/todd-simmons-55364412_north-carolina-at-students-march-back-to-ugcPost-7516656540976795649-Vavy": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:52:19.965819+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Clarification: On Thursday, Oct. 15, thousands of Aggie students took part in TWO major marches to downtown Greensboro:\n\n- The first was a March to the Polls, as previously described, which went from campus to the Union Square polling location downtown on the first day of early voting in North Carolina. Students marched back to campus after voting in protest of the Guilford County Elections Board's removal of their campus early voting polling location earlier this year.\n\n- The second was a March for Justice for Nolan Wells, the 18-year-old young man who tragically died July 4 under murky circumstances in the waters off Mississippi’s Horn Island after celebrating the Independence Day holiday. The march was organized by the A&T chapter of the NAACP, and a coalition of groups worked tirelessly to bring students together in solidarity for Nolan from across campus and the entire state. The march began at A&T’s February One monument, went downtown to the International Civil Rights Museum and returned to campus.\n\nIncredibly, thousands of Aggies took part in *both* marches, but in the video posted here, were returning from the second march, which concluded later. In both instances, outstanding civic leadership and participation were on full display from A&T students in the best tradition of Aggies, who have been leading in important community events since the university’s establishment in 1891. \n\nA&T continues to be America's largest HBCU, as well as its top-rated public HBCU in Forbes and US News & World Report.",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/trmlabs_at-2005-utc-on-october-29-approximately-activity-7521757016516628480-UBCU": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:52:19.965819+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "At 20:05 UTC on October 29, approximately USD 6.36 billion began moving out of Binance wallets across ten blockchains, most of it in about 20 minutes. It is the largest crypto theft on record, roughly four times the Bybit hack of February 2025.\n\nTRM Labs attributes the attack to TraderTraitor, North Korea’s elite state-sponsored hacking unit, based on robust on-chain and off-chain intelligence. The same group was named by the FBI in the Bybit hack, and the staging, the Tornado Cash funding and the pre-signed transactions all match earlier North Korea-linked heists.\n\nThe response has been fast. Tether, Circle, Ripple, World Liberty Financial and Arbitrum’s Security Council have frozen roughly USD 2.7 billion. But the attacker still controls about USD 2.4 billion in assets beyond any issuer’s reach, and is racing to convert and move them.\n\nTRM continues to work with Binance and the Beacon Network to track the funds and alert partners in real time. The story is still developing, and we will share more as the investigation unfolds.\n\nRead our full analysis: https://lnkd.in/e-9KjvPB",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-30T02:17:00.224Z"
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T19:52:19.965819+00:00"
  },
